{{ define "title" }}Privacy Policy{{ end }}

{{ define "main" }}
  <main class="w-full bg-slate-50" data-page="privacy">
    <header class="bg-slate-900">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-screen-xl px-3 py-10 md:px-6 md:py-12">
        <p
          class="mb-3 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-orange-500"
        >
          Legal
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white sm:text-5xl">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-300">
          Last updated: November 17, 2026
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-7 text-slate-100">
          This policy explains how theSketchDB collects, uses, and protects
          information when you use our website.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <article class="mx-auto w-full max-w-screen-xl px-3 py-8 md:px-6 md:py-12">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-9 text-base leading-7 text-slate-700">
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            1. Information we collect
          </h2>
          <p>
            When you create an account, we may collect your username, email
            address, and information needed to authenticate you. If you sign in
            with Google, we receive basic account information made available
            through the sign-in process, such as your Google account identifier,
            name, and email address. We do not receive your Google password.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We also store information you choose to provide through the service,
            including sketch favorites and ratings. Basic technical information,
            such as IP addresses and browser information, may be processed in
            server logs for security and troubleshooting.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            2. How we use information
          </h2>
          <p>
            We use this information to create and manage accounts, authenticate
            sign-ins, provide features such as favorites and ratings, maintain
            site security, troubleshoot problems, and communicate about
            account-related matters.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            3. Google sign-in
          </h2>
          <p>
            Google sign-in is used to verify your identity and associate your
            Google account with your theSketchDB account. We use Google account
            information for authentication and account management, not to access
            your Gmail, Google Drive, or other Google content.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            4. Cookies and sessions
          </h2>
          <p>
            We use cookies or similar technologies necessary to keep you signed
            in and maintain your session. You can manage cookies through your
            browser settings, although disabling essential cookies may prevent
            account features from working.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            5. Sharing and service providers
          </h2>
          <p>
            We do not sell your personal information. We may share information
            with providers that help us host, secure, and operate the service,
            only as needed to provide those services. We may also disclose
            information when required by law or to protect the service and its
            users.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            6. Visibility of account activity
          </h2>
          <p>
            Your username and any profile information or activity you choose to
            make public may be visible to others. Features that allow sharing
            favorites or ratings will follow the visibility settings offered by
            the service.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            7. Retention and security
          </h2>
          <p>
            We retain account information for as long as needed to operate your
            account and meet legitimate security or legal requirements. We use
            reasonable measures to protect information, but no internet service
            can guarantee absolute security.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            8. Your choices
          </h2>
          <p>
            You may contact us to request access to, correction of, or deletion
            of your account information. Some records may be retained when
            necessary for security or legal compliance.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
            9. Changes to this policy
          </h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy as the service changes. We will post the
            revised policy here and update the date above.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">10. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For privacy questions or account data requests, email
            <a
              class="font-medium text-orange-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-orange-600"
              href="mailto:support@thesketchdb.com"
              >support@thesketchdb.com</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
      <footer class="mt-10 max-w-3xl border-t border-slate-200 pt-6 text-sm">
        <a href="/terms" class="font-bold text-orange-700 hover:text-orange-600"
          >Read our Terms of Service &rarr;</a
        >
      </footer>
    </article>
  </main>
{{ end }}
